<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mubadala Investment Company</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2002">2002</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mubadala Investment Company is a sovereign wealth fund owned by the government of Abu Dhabi. Founded in 2002 as Mubadala Development Company and merged with the International Petroleum Investment Company in 2017, it invests worldwide in sectors such as energy, technology, aerospace and health care, helping to diversify the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a>'s economy away from oil.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Through the Abu Dhabi Investment Authority, <b>Mubadala</b> and other funds the country became a major investor worldwide.</blockquote><a href="/empire/united-arab-emirates">United Arab Emirates · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li></ul></section>
